.TH LIBMPQ__ARCHIVE_OPEN_IO 3 2026-09-24 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__archive_open_io \- open an MPQ archive through random-access I/O.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B
#include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__archive_open_io("
.BI "        mpq_archive_s **" "mpq_archive,"
.BI "        void            *" "context,"
.BI "        libmpq_read_at_fn " "read_at,"
.BI "        libmpq__off_t    " "source_size,"
.BI "        libmpq__off_t    " "archive_offset,"
.BI "        const char       *" "source_name"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Open an MPQ through an exact random-access callback. A zero callback result
means that the callback populated the full requested buffer. Negative
\fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_*\fP results report failure. libmpq can request absolute
offsets in arbitrary order, performs each range check against
\fIsource_size\fP before dispatch, and reports positive callback results as
\fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_READ\fP. The callback runs synchronously and must not retain
the buffer.
.PP
The context and callback are borrowed. They must remain valid until this
archive and every clone are closed. libmpq never frees context or closes a
caller-owned resource; callers provide synchronization for shared contexts.
Set \fIarchive_offset\fP to -1 to scan for an embedded header.
.PP
\fIsource_name\fP is optional and copied by libmpq as the logical archive
name. Its basename is used for legacy strong-signature verification. When it
is NULL, basename-dependent strong signatures are skipped; plain and ARCHIVE
strong variants remain available.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, *\fImpq_archive\fP receives a new \fBmpq_archive_s\fP and zero is
returned. On failure, the output handle is NULL. In addition to reader/parser
errors, \fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST\fP reports a NULL output or callback,
\fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_SIZE\fP reports a negative source size, and
\fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_SEEK\fP reports an invalid explicit archive offset.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq__archive_open_mpqe_io (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_clone (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_close (3)
